Ottoline: Forty years I judged the county fair. The marrows were bigger then, but the people are braver now.
- What are you selling?
	Ottoline: Pies, honey, cheese. Things to inspire you, dear.
	[signal arg="shop:festival"]
- How does judging work?
	Ottoline: Bring three things you grew, cooked or made. The finer and rarer, the better. Gold-star quality counts extra.
	Ottoline: You keep them, of course. I only look. And sniff. Occasionally taste.
	[signal arg="open:showcase"]
- What wins?
	Ottoline: Something only you could have brought. Last year it was a truffle. The year before, a perfect melon.
- Maybe later.
	Ottoline: The table is open until five.
